.TH LIBESDM_ES_EXT 3 "2026-11-06" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
libesdm_es_ext \- external entropy sources for the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <esdm/esdm_es_ext.h>
.PP
.BI "int esdm_es_ext_provider_main(const struct esdm_es_ext_plugin *" plugin ", int " argc ", char *" argv "[]);"
.PP
.B pkg\-config \-\-cflags \-\-libs esdm_es_ext
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
An external entropy source is served to
.BR esdm\-server (8)
by a provider: a process of its own on a UNIX domain socket, which the ESDM
reads with
.B \-\-es_ext
.IR PATH .
No code of a source runs in the ESDM: a source that crashes takes its
provider down, and the ESDM connects again once it is back.
.PP
A provider is the callbacks of a
.B struct esdm_es_ext_plugin
\- documented in
.I esdm_es_ext.h
\- and a
.BR main ()
returning
.BR esdm_es_ext_provider_main ().
Only
.B get_entropy
is required;
.BR init ,
.BR fini ,
.BR selftest ,
.B status_json
and
.B entropy_rate
are optional, and
.B name
names the source in the ESDM status. The callbacks are never called
concurrently.
.SS Entropy credit
A block is credited with the entropy the source claims for it \- a claim
beyond the data is refused \- at most at the rate configured in the ESDM
.RB ( \-\-es_ext_entropy_rate ),
else at the one the source declares, else at 0. The provider must run as root
or as the user the ESDM accepts
.RB ( \-\-es_ext_uid ):
accepting that user means trusting the rate it declares. A new connection is
credited only after a self test passed.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.BR esdm_es_ext_provider_main ()
takes the command line, sets the source up and serves it until SIGTERM,
SIGINT or SIGHUP; it tells systemd once it serves
.RB ( Type=notify ).
.PP
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_alloc (),
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_allow_uid (),
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_set_name (),
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_set_entropy_rate (),
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_run (),
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_stop ()
and
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_free ()
serve a source from a program of its own making, see
.IR esdm_es_ext.h .
The server serves up to 8 clients, a new one taking the slot of the one idle
the longest \- of root only for another one of root.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR esdm_es_ext_provider_main ()
returns 0 once a signal ended it, or for
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version ,
and 1 otherwise. The server functions return 0 or a negative errno, but for
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_stop ()
and
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_free (),
which return nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
The socket to serve on, replacing a socket there, but no other file.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Its access mode, octal, 0666 by default. Every user who can connect can fill
the backlog the ESDM connects through: a group of the ESDM user is safer.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-client_uid " \fIUSER\fR"
Serve clients running as
.I USER
next to root, up to 8 times; nobody by default, the user the ESDM runs as.
Every process of the user can take a client slot from the ESDM: a user only the
ESDM runs as is safer.
.TP
.BR \-\-name " \fINAME\fR"
Declare
.I NAME
\- 1 to 32 bytes of UTF-8 without control characters \- in place of the name
of the source.
.TP
.BR \-\-entropy_rate " \fIBITS\fR"
Declare
.I BITS
per 256 bits of data, 0 to 256, in place of the rate of the source.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
More verbose logging, repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-\-version
Print the usage or the version.
.SH STATUS
The ESDM shows the status of a provider as the
.B provider
member of its source. That of this library is
.PP
.nf
{ "server": { "version": ..., "plugin_api": 1, "name": ...,
  "entropy_rate": ..., "clients": 1, "client_slots": 8, "requests": 42,
  "selftest": "passed", "uptime_seconds": 3600 }, "plugin": ... }
.fi
.PP
.B plugin
being what
.B status_json
reports: a JSON object of up to 512 bytes, nested up to 8 levels, without
NaN, infinities, C1 or bidirectional controls \- null otherwise.
.SH PROTOCOL
The socket protocol \- one protobuf message of
.I es\-ext/pb/es_ext.proto
per datagram \- is documented in
.I esdm_es_ext.h
for providers written without the library.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <errno.h>
#include <esdm/esdm_es_ext.h>

static int my_get_entropy(void *ctx, uint8_t *buf, size_t buflen,
			  uint32_t *entropy_bits)
{
	if (read_my_noise_source(buf, buflen))
		return \-EIO;
	*entropy_bits = buflen; /* the assessment: 1 bit per byte */
	return 0;
}

static const struct esdm_es_ext_plugin my_source = {
	.version = ESDM_ES_EXT_PLUGIN_VERSION,
	.name = "my\-noise\-source",
	.get_entropy = my_get_entropy,
};

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
	return esdm_es_ext_provider_main(&my_source, argc, argv);
}
.fi
.PP
.nf
cc \-o my\-provider my_provider.c $(pkg\-config \-\-cflags \-\-libs esdm_es_ext)
my\-provider \-\-socket /run/my\-es.socket
esdm\-server \-\-es_ext /run/my\-es.socket
.fi
.PP
.I es\-ext/example/esdm_es_ext_example.c
is a complete one.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-es\-pkcs11 (8),
.BR esdm\-es\-pcsc (8),
.BR libesdm (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Markus Theil <theil.markus@gmail.com>
